+- [MAJOR] project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py:2140 -> the store is selected only by family even though the spec requires sessions per `route_id`; an enabled run that switches between two OPENAI (or ANTHROPIC) routes resumes the other route's transcript and credentials/model context. The driven call resumed `old-route-session` for a new route -> key/look up records by `(family, route_id)` (or reject a route-id mismatch) before deriving resume argv -> @owner
+- [MAJOR] project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py:2197 -> the governing hash omits the loaded `adjudicate-*` prompt templates, so changing a judging instruction does not drain the retained session as required. A driven launch before and after changing `prompts/adjudicate-disposition.md` returned the same hash -> resolve and pass the actual loaded adjudication template paths into `governing_hash`, with an integration regression test -> @owner
+- [MAJOR] project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py:2866 -> OPENAI and OPENCODE never invoke the new occupancy/session-id readers: `family_context_telemetry` returns blanks for both, so bookkeeping persists an empty session id and every later launch mints rather than resumes. The driven OPENAI bookkeeping/launch produced `["codex", "exec", "--json"]`, `resumed=True`, and `session_id=''` -> wire each family's emitted JSON/rollout source through its reader and persist the captured id before enabling the dial -> @owner
+- [MINOR] docs/requirements/interfaces.toml:1119 -> IF-174's `Rationale` cites WI-540/plan history, contrary to the registry stand-alone rule -> replace the citation frame with the standing reason and leave provenance in the process record -> @owner
+- [MINOR] docs/requirements/interfaces.toml:1123 -> IF-174 `Data` is 250 characters (over the declared 160-character ceiling) and names the runtime-only `out/adjudicator` path as a source-surface datum -> reduce it to a typed interface alphabet/schema pointer and put the definition in the owner contract -> @owner
+- [MINOR] project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicator_session.py:1 -> the new IF-174 owner declares neither `Contracts: IF-174` nor a `Contract IF-174:` body, leaving the added seam unstated and untraceable from its owner -> add the header declaration and the single contract body -> @owner
+VERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=6
